            <div xml:id="d539">

                <pb facs="0708" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">365D.1163/45: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-09T14:00:00+03:00">February 9, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. Please see last paragraph of my 690, December 22, 3 p.m.<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d539-f1"/> Within the past few days the Italian authorities have
                    again been making active preparations to take over the mission property. I have
                    advised the mission to present to the authorities a statement as to the value of
                    all its movable and immovable properties together with a complete inventory.</p>
                <p>Has the Department any instructions beyond those contained in: its 398, December
                    8, 5 p.m.?<anchor n="13" xml:id="d539-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
